## HUD states

From public guides, not checked on a real frame. What the Core could read in
each, at 1080p:

| state | what is on screen | what the Core could read |
|---|---|---|
| Hero select | Grid of hero portraits by role, the picked hero large with its name, team-up icons | The hero's **name as text** and the portrait: the one moment the hero is named on screen. Also re-opened mid-match when the player swaps at spawn |
| In play | Ability icons with key labels bottom-right, ultimate circle bottom-centre (percentage, glows when ready), ammo count near the abilities for heroes with ammo, health bottom-left, team portraits top, kill feed top-right | The **ability row** (icon set identifies the hero, D122), the ammo counter, the ultimate charge. No hero or attack name as text |
| Ultimate active | Ultimate effects, often a changed ability row or a timer; some (Black Widow's Assassin's Focus, Gorr's Twilight of the Gods) change the primary attack | The ultimate circle draining, the swapped row |
| Transformations / forms | Whole ability row swaps: Hulk's three forms, Cloak & Dagger, Emma Frost's Diamond Form, Magik's Darkchild, White Fox Awakened / Kumiho Form, The Hood's Half-Demon State, Deadpool guns / katanas, Angela, Elsa | The **row change** is the most readable sign of a form; teach each form's own row |
| Loki's ultimate | Loki takes another hero's whole HUD | Reads as that other hero: a known false positive |
| Dead / respawn | Death recap, kill cam, respawn timer, spectating a teammate (their HUD), a hero-swap prompt | Respawn timer; **no own HUD**. Spectate shows someone else's row: hold off |
| Menus | Main menu, lobby, scoreboard (Tab), settings, end-of-match screens | Nothing to act on; the absence of the in-play row |

"HUD Widget Size" in settings scales the HUD and the HUD can be hidden, so a
taught row is per player setting.

## Class: Rainbow-style

**Rainbow-style** (hero-picker driven), not name-reading. Evidence: the hero
is named as text only at hero select; in play neither the hero nor the attack
is printed, only the ability-icon row, the ammo counter and the ultimate
circle (guides and the HUD-settings descriptions above, not a real frame).
So the owner picks the hero in the app (or the Core recognises the taught
ability row, D122), and each form's row is taught for the heroes listed
under "The attacks". Name reading has nothing to read in play.

## Update the list when a season adds a hero

Check the new name on https://www.marvelrivals.com/heroes/ and the season's
announcement; add the hero at the end of his role's group (the build sorts by
name) with `loadout.attacks`, each attack in the role's attack group with
`usedBy`; set `asOf` and `season`; run
`node dashboard/tools/test-game-data.js`.
